Z||000000||kanada||05-01-2001||10:57 AM||||i got hit from behind the other day<P>there is no real damage but the paint chiped off in two places, is the paint on fieros different?  what kind of paint should i be looking for to repair these spots?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PKFieroGT||05-01-2001||11:12 AM||||I just had my rear bumper cover repaired after I was hit in the rear passenger side. The damage wasn't too bad other than cosmetic paint cracking a chipping off. The bottom line was that it cost the insurance company $750 to fix Canadian$$  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>The guys that fixed it said that it had been repaired before and that whoever did it did not put enough "flex" compond in the paint, which is why it cracked and chipped. When you get it painted and repaired make sure the guys who do it realize that it's a flexible component. In my case, he said that all that should have happened was that the paint should have "spidered" (ie cracked like a spider web). That way, the repair would have been easier. Just my 2cents..<P>PKFieroGT||||reg||10
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-01-2001||03:34 PM||||theres lots of previous threads on FLEX additive.Do a search. My short story on it is dont waste your time and money. I never use it ever. Ive been in body business for 30? years. Owned my own for last 15. PK, the reason the original factory paint job bends so much without cracking is the factory didnt 'paint' them, it was a flexible coating that was applied where the bumpers were manufactured. No body shop anywhere is equiped to duplicate it. The paint is gonna crack when you bend it very far, even if you put a gallon of flex in your paint.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
